{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012CNewM9hDK55ezwF1nSdJY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D08 released; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. day 19 released D01-D03, day 20 D04-D05,\n5\t  day 21 D06-D08 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is NOT always the title: D07 \"Stored for Later\"\n6\t  = `web-exploitation-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`). Expect ~3 lane-days per\n7\t  calendar day. Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR\n8\t  \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing\n9\t  function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for\n10\t  Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read\n11\t  -> access control -> client-side (XSS x2) -> session management.\n12\t- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n13\t  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n14\t  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n15\t- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n16\t  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app.\n17\t- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n18\t  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel/`X-Powered-By: PHP/8.3`, Node, FastAPI-style\n19\t  `/openapi.json`). `GET /api/clues` (linked as \"Open workspace notes\") names everything: `framework`,\n20\t  `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `secondary_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ONE\n21\t  concept-specific key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`). Routes\n22\t  answer machine-readable JSON errors that say what is missing (`session_id_required`,\n23\t  `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\n24\t  \"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`.\n25\t- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06: NO real browser -- the server accepts a request that LOOKS\n26\t  browser-originated from the reflected page (fetch-metadata headers + Referer). D07: a REAL moderator browser bot\n27\t  visits stored content a few seconds (sometimes >12 s) later and runs your script with its cookies.\n28\t- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 for D08**); the prompt\n29\t  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery / compounding so far: D01 (x2), D02, D04, D05. Mastery\n30\t  targets can take ~5 min in `preparing` (singles / TT 4-10 s).\n31\t\n32\t## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n33\t- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n34\t  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n35\t- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n36\t  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), then run the concept probes the recon hints first, the rest\n37\t  after. Earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY -- day-21 solvers' `fallback()`s import each other (infinite recursion =\n38\t  timeout). Running every probe at once x3 targets slowed each 2-5x: stage them.\n39\t- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action`; secondary\n40\t  `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `staff-<hex8>`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`,\n41\t  `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value (D06 TT broke on `/internal-`).\n42\t- **Resource noun on boards** (D07): `/api/messages` + `/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}`.\n43\t  Rule: take the submit route and the `/<noun>/{id}` view from `/openapi.json` `paths` / the submit response's\n44\t  `url`, else the home page (it lists every entry with its receipt).\n45\t- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file\n46\t  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2\n47\t  same-origin crawl from robots/sitemap/comments, regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.\n48\t- **IDOR (D02)**: foreign ids in `/api/history`; API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: request foreign ids.\n49\t- **SQLi (D03)**: `/lookup?q=` wrapped in `('%..%')`. Rule: tautologies covering `'` `')` `'))` `\"` + `--`/`#`.\n50\t- **LFI (D04)**: `reader.php?doc=<page>`, prompt-named `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: every param with `.`/`/`\n51\t  in its value x `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, `<orig dir>/`+`../`*10.\n52\t- **Access control (D05)**: GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON.\n53\t- **Proof carrier**: HTML text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`, a receipt shown on a board page. Rule:\n54\t  regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- don't key on field names.\n55\t\n56\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n57\t- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n58\t  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n59\t- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login, browser).\n60\t- `Disallow:` / \"crawler policy\" comment -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR.\n61\t- Search form / \"database\" -> D03 tautology. `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal.\n62\t- \"staff-only door, just a sign\", `feature_route` -> D05 GET it.\n63\t- \"repeats everything you tell it\", \"talks back\", `callback_nonce` -> D06: reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')\n64\t  </script>` via `?q=` on the feature route, then GET the callback yourself with browser headers.\n65\t- \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", \"good things come to those who wait\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07: store a\n66\t  script that fetches the data route and POSTs it to the receipt route; poll the entry page.\n67\t- \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", \"somebody else's credentials\", `session_hint` -> D08 session fixation.\n68\t- JSON with `effect` + `evidence` = landed; `evidence` is the answer.\n69\t\n70\t## Day by day\n71\t- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**, compressed: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery D04 missed\n72\t  it: crawl only one level deep). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1\n73\t  --` (plain `' OR '1'='1` failed: paren-wrapped). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt` (absolute\n74\t  and `....//` failed); single 51 s. D05 `/api/clues` -> GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `effect:\n75\t  framework_authorization_bypassed`; single 47 s, Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing).\n76\t- **D06 Reflect Upon This (cal. 21)** -- reflected XSS with a server-judged \"isolated callback\". Clues:\n77\t  `feature_route` (`/execute-<hex6>` | `/process-<hex6>`, reflects `?q=` raw into `<div id=\"preview\">`),\n78\t  `secondary_route` (`/callback-<hex6>` | `/internal-<hex6>`), `callback_nonce` (12 hex). A bare GET of the callback\n79\t  -> `{\"error\":\"browser_callback_required\"}`. Worked: GET `<feature>?q=<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>`\n80\t  (confirms reflection), then GET `<cb>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, `Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors`,\n81\t  `Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty`, `Referer: <the reflected URL>`, `Origin: <base>`, `X-Callback-Nonce: N` -> `effect:\n82\t  isolated_browser_callback`. No real browser needed. Single CORRECT 83 s. **TT had trouble**: solver chose the\n83\t  callback by the word `callback` in the route value; TT's was `/internal-<hex6>` (2 generalize workers) -> pick by\n84\t  key `secondary_route`.\n85\t- **D07 Stored for Later (cal. 21)** -- stored XSS executed by a real moderator bot. Clues: `moderator_data_route`\n86\t  (`/staff-<hex8>`, 401/403 for us) + `receipt_route_template` (`/api/<noun>/{id}/receipt-<hex6>`). Worked: POST JSON\n87\t  `{\"message\":\"<script>(async()=>{t=await(await fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'})).text();await fetch(RCPT(id),\n88\t  {method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({evidence:t})})})()</script>\",\n89\t  \"name\":\"guest\"}` to `/api/messages` -> `{id,url}`; the entry id is read from `location.pathname` inside the script;\n90\t  poll `/messages/{id}` until the receipt shows the proof. Single CORRECT 78 s. **Mastery had trouble**: Target 2\n91\t  used `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}` and the solver polled `/messages/{id}` (404) -> derive the view from\n92\t  openapi/submit response/home; its receipt also landed AFTER the 12 s poll window (poll longer on untimed runs,\n93\t  re-read the board at the end). A compounding D04 LFI target timed out on solver mutual recursion (fixed:\n94\t  `answer()` only). Mastery submit got HTTP 503 `temporarily_unavailable` although the GM had registered CORRECT;\n95\t  the retry said `already_solved` -> check `hctf status` after a 503 before retrying.\n96\t- **D08 Session Impression (cal. 21)** -- session fixation (\"Laravel\", PHP). Clues: `feature_route: /action-<hex6>`\n97\t  (planting route), `secondary_route: /status-<hex6>` (bare -> 403 `authenticated_login_required`), `session_hint:\n98\t  <12 hex>`. Bare `/action-*` -> 400 `session_id_required`; `?session=`, `?session_id=`, JSON body, `X-Session-Id`,\n99\t  `laravel_session`/`session` cookies all failed; `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<session_hint>` -> `{\"ok\":true,\n100\t  \"session_established\":true}` + `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` (the victim then logs in on that id). Then `GET\n101\t  /status-<hex6>` with `Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> `effect: fixed_session_privilege_transfer`. Single CORRECT\n102\t  116 s. **Mastery had trouble** (3 targets incl. a D05 target, ~15 min, 3 generalize workers): racing every earlier\n103\t  solver on all targets at once starved the app (5 s -> 13 s); fixed by running today's probe alone when the clues\n104\t  carry a `sess|sid` key and staging the rest by recon hints. An unverified variant (`expected.json` = `{}`) can't go\n105\t  green in solver-test -- that's harness bookkeeping, not a solver bug.\n106\t\n107\t## GM answer conventions learned\n108\t- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n109\t  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n110\t- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n111\t  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08). D07 shows the proof in a moderator receipt on the entry page instead.\n112\t- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n113\t\n114\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n115\t- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (`callback`, `messages`) -- words are re-dealt; use clue keys / openapi.\n116\t- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: earlier-day targets get today's prompt (D04 missed T1).\n117\t- One-level crawls: the D01 proof sits one link below the Disallow index.\n118\t- Solvers importing each other's `fallback()` -> mutual recursion -> timeout. Import `answer()` only.\n119\t- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n120\t- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n121\t- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n122\t- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n123\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a36620c-cc4e-43c4-b504-292458b62d8d","uuid":"558afebe-01dd-4682-b7cb-03009a9b5ae1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:09:29.945Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D08 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. day 19 released D01-D03, day 20 D04-D05,\n  day 21 D06-D08 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is NOT always the title: D07 \"Stored for Later\"\n  = `web-exploitation-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`). Expect ~3 lane-days per\n  calendar day. Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR\n  \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing\n  function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for\n  Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read\n  -> access control -> client-side (XSS x2) -> session management.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel/`X-Powered-By: PHP/8.3`, Node, FastAPI-style\n  `/openapi.json`). `GET /api/clues` (linked as \"Open workspace notes\") names everything: `framework`,\n  `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `secondary_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ONE\n  concept-specific key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`). Routes\n  answer machine-readable JSON errors that say what is missing (`session_id_required`,\n  `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\n  \"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06: NO real browser -- the server accepts a request that LOOKS\n  browser-originated from the reflected page (fetch-metadata headers + Referer). D07: a REAL moderator browser bot\n  visits stored content a few seconds (sometimes >12 s) later and runs your script with its cookies.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 for D08**); the prompt\n  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery / compounding so far: D01 (x2), D02, D04, D05. Mastery\n  targets can take ~5 min in `preparing` (singles / TT 4-10 s).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), then run the concept probes the recon hints first, the rest\n  after. Earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY -- day-21 solvers' `fallback()`s import each other (infinite recursion =\n  timeout). Running every probe at once x3 targets slowed each 2-5x: stage them.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action`; secondary\n  `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `staff-<hex8>`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`,\n  `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value (D06 TT broke on `/internal-`).\n- **Resource noun on boards** (D07): `/api/messages` + `/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}`.\n  Rule: take the submit route and the `/<noun>/{id}` view from `/openapi.json` `paths` / the submit response's\n  `url`, else the home page (it lists every entry with its receipt).\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file\n  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2\n  same-origin crawl from robots/sitemap/comments, regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.\n- **IDOR (D02)**: foreign ids in `/api/history`; API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: request foreign ids.\n- **SQLi (D03)**: `/lookup?q=` wrapped in `('%..%')`. Rule: tautologies covering `'` `')` `'))` `\"` + `--`/`#`.\n- **LFI (D04)**: `reader.php?doc=<page>`, prompt-named `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: every param with `.`/`/`\n  in its value x `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, `<orig dir>/`+`../`*10.\n- **Access control (D05)**: GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`, a receipt shown on a board page. Rule:\n  regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- don't key on field names.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login, browser).\n- `Disallow:` / \"crawler policy\" comment -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR.\n- Search form / \"database\" -> D03 tautology. `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal.\n- \"staff-only door, just a sign\", `feature_route` -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything you tell it\", \"talks back\", `callback_nonce` -> D06: reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')\n  </script>` via `?q=` on the feature route, then GET the callback yourself with browser headers.\n- \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", \"good things come to those who wait\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07: store a\n  script that fetches the data route and POSTs it to the receipt route; poll the entry page.\n- \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", \"somebody else's credentials\", `session_hint` -> D08 session fixation.\n- JSON with `effect` + `evidence` = landed; `evidence` is the answer.\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**, compressed: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery D04 missed\n  it: crawl only one level deep). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1\n  --` (plain `' OR '1'='1` failed: paren-wrapped). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt` (absolute\n  and `....//` failed); single 51 s. D05 `/api/clues` -> GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `effect:\n  framework_authorization_bypassed`; single 47 s, Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing).\n- **D06 Reflect Upon This (cal. 21)** -- reflected XSS with a server-judged \"isolated callback\". Clues:\n  `feature_route` (`/execute-<hex6>` | `/process-<hex6>`, reflects `?q=` raw into `<div id=\"preview\">`),\n  `secondary_route` (`/callback-<hex6>` | `/internal-<hex6>`), `callback_nonce` (12 hex). A bare GET of the callback\n  -> `{\"error\":\"browser_callback_required\"}`. Worked: GET `<feature>?q=<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>`\n  (confirms reflection), then GET `<cb>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, `Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors`,\n  `Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty`, `Referer: <the reflected URL>`, `Origin: <base>`, `X-Callback-Nonce: N` -> `effect:\n  isolated_browser_callback`. No real browser needed. Single CORRECT 83 s. **TT had trouble**: solver chose the\n  callback by the word `callback` in the route value; TT's was `/internal-<hex6>` (2 generalize workers) -> pick by\n  key `secondary_route`.\n- **D07 Stored for Later (cal. 21)** -- stored XSS executed by a real moderator bot. Clues: `moderator_data_route`\n  (`/staff-<hex8>`, 401/403 for us) + `receipt_route_template` (`/api/<noun>/{id}/receipt-<hex6>`). Worked: POST JSON\n  `{\"message\":\"<script>(async()=>{t=await(await fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'})).text();await fetch(RCPT(id),\n  {method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({evidence:t})})})()</script>\",\n  \"name\":\"guest\"}` to `/api/messages` -> `{id,url}`; the entry id is read from `location.pathname` inside the script;\n  poll `/messages/{id}` until the receipt shows the proof. Single CORRECT 78 s. **Mastery had trouble**: Target 2\n  used `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}` and the solver polled `/messages/{id}` (404) -> derive the view from\n  openapi/submit response/home; its receipt also landed AFTER the 12 s poll window (poll longer on untimed runs,\n  re-read the board at the end). A compounding D04 LFI target timed out on solver mutual recursion (fixed:\n  `answer()` only). Mastery submit got HTTP 503 `temporarily_unavailable` although the GM had registered CORRECT;\n  the retry said `already_solved` -> check `hctf status` after a 503 before retrying.\n- **D08 Session Impression (cal. 21)** -- session fixation (\"Laravel\", PHP). Clues: `feature_route: /action-<hex6>`\n  (planting route), `secondary_route: /status-<hex6>` (bare -> 403 `authenticated_login_required`), `session_hint:\n  <12 hex>`. Bare `/action-*` -> 400 `session_id_required`; `?session=`, `?session_id=`, JSON body, `X-Session-Id`,\n  `laravel_session`/`session` cookies all failed; `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<session_hint>` -> `{\"ok\":true,\n  \"session_established\":true}` + `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` (the victim then logs in on that id). Then `GET\n  /status-<hex6>` with `Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> `effect: fixed_session_privilege_transfer`. Single CORRECT\n  116 s. **Mastery had trouble** (3 targets incl. a D05 target, ~15 min, 3 generalize workers): racing every earlier\n  solver on all targets at once starved the app (5 s -> 13 s); fixed by running today's probe alone when the clues\n  carry a `sess|sid` key and staging the rest by recon hints. An unverified variant (`expected.json` = `{}`) can't go\n  green in solver-test -- that's harness bookkeeping, not a solver bug.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08). D07 shows the proof in a moderator receipt on the entry page instead.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (`callback`, `messages`) -- words are re-dealt; use clue keys / openapi.\n- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: earlier-day targets get today's prompt (D04 missed T1).\n- One-level crawls: the D01 proof sits one link below the Disallow index.\n- Solvers importing each other's `fallback()` -> mutual recursion -> timeout. Import `answer()` only.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n","numLines":123,"startLine":1,"totalLines":123}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012CNewM9hDK55ezwF1nSdJY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
