{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DQbsBDVWwmAueQGdFymkzC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Web coverage atlas\n2\t\n3\tLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\n4\tquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\n5\tclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\n6\ttraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\n7\tcallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation. Since D05 every target is the same kit:\n8\t`/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `current_role` + one concept key (`callback_nonce`,\n9\t`moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`); routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece;\n10\tsuccess = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Mastery = today's bug + 1-2 earlier lane-days\n11\t(2 targets D03-D07, 3 on D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: ~3 lane-days per calendar day (D01-D03 cal.\n12\t19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21) -> priority 1 below = the ~9 bugs most likely in D09-D17.\n13\tArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\n14\tsession management. D08 opened the auth/session family and D07 proved a real victim browser exists, so the next\n15\tmost likely are: CSRF (bot victim), JWT / signed-cookie forgery, DOM XSS, open redirect, role tampering, then the\n16\tserver-side classics (command injection, SSTI, SSRF, XXE, upload, deserialization).\n17\tSnapshot 2026-10-21 (after D08). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and there is no `lib/web.py`; no `web:*` keys\n18\tin `.run/prebuild-state.json` (gap `enable-web-prebuild-lane`).\n19\t\n20\tStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n21\t`gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan\n22\t`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n23\t\n24\t## Coverage table\n25\t\n26\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n29\t| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n30\t| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n31\t| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n32\t| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n33\t| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie | flip the value the app names | high |\n34\t| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high (session family after D08) |\n35\t| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n36\t| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET only | add `role:\"admin\"` to PUT/POST | high |\n37\t| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | high |\n38\t| 11 | SSTI | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | high |\n39\t| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | high |\n40\t| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n41\t| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n42\t| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high (XSS trilogy) |\n43\t| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med-high |\n44\t| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n45\t| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n46\t| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n47\t| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml` | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |\n48\t| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med |\n49\t| 20 | file upload -> execution / traversal | gap | upload form, files served back | executable type or `../` filename | med |\n50\t| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med-low |\n51\t| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n52\t| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n53\t| 24a | CSRF (bot victim performs a state change) | gap | \"the admin clicks links\", \"change email\", no token / SameSite=None, report-to-admin | host an auto-submitting form / fetch in stored content or a bot-visited URL | high (bot proven D07; session family D08) |\n54\t| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | med-high |\n55\t| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker; bot reads data | med |\n56\t| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n57\t| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |\n58\t| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\" | parallel burst, negative values | med-low |\n59\t| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n60\t| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n61\t| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n62\t| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n63\t| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint`, 400 `session_id_required` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie `arena_session=<hint>` on secondary | done; Mastery |\n64\t| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs/Referer | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med (D08 sequel) |\n65\t| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n66\t\n67\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n68\t\n69\t```\n70\tFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n71\t  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ONE concept key (see table below)\n72\t  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n73\t      browser_callback_required, 401/403 = needs the victim's/admin's session)\n74\t  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n75\t  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). JSON `evidence` = answer.\n76\t  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\n77\tPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\n78\tvalue (callback|internal|status, messages|postcards are re-dealt per variant).\n79\tMASTERY: 2-3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n80\t\n81\tCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n82\trobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n83\t\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\n84\tsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)\n85\t?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\n86\tfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\n87\tcallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n88\t      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty,\n89\t      Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin: <base>, X-Callback-Nonce: N   -> effect isolated_browser_callback\n90\tmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,\n91\t  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          {credentials:'include'}) -> POST RCPT(id from location.pathname)\n92\t                                                            {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} and / for >=30 s\n93\tsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n94\t                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\n95\tcurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin\n96\teyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n97\t\"admin clicks links\", \"change email\", report-to-admin  -> CSRF               -> stored/bot-visited auto-submit form to the state route\n98\tlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n99\t?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n100\t\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n101\t\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read\n102\t\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n103\t\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\n104\tXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n105\tA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\n106\treceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser required\" errors without a bot (D06) = send fetch-metadata headers yourself.\n107\tBanners (\"Django\", \"Laravel\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\t## Readiness gaps\n111\t\n112\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python in a\n113\tfuture `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded\n114\tbodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no web prebuild lane).\n115\t\n116\t```json\n117\t[\n118\t  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D08: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and lib/web.py does not exist, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n119\t  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + JSON error codes to the concept and the next request (rows 5, 13a, 13b, 31)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs.\"},\n120\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n121\t  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n122\t  {\"id\": \"csrf-bot-planner\", \"concept\": \"CSRF executed by the app's victim bot (row 24a)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D07 proved the GM runs a real moderator browser. CSRF sequel: find the state-changing route (clues *_route, openapi POST/PUT without a token field, forms lacking csrf inputs, cookies SameSite=None/Lax), build (a) an auto-submitting HTML form (GET and POST, urlencoded and text/plain JSON trick) and (b) a fetch(...,{credentials:'include'}) script, deliver it where the bot looks (stored entry, report/share URL endpoint, profile field), then poll the clue/status route or the entry page for the receipt/effect. Token bypasses: drop the token, empty token, token from our own session, GET instead of POST, method override.\"},\n123\t  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n124\t  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile route (mass assignment). Parser: effect+evidence JSON or proof regex.\"},\n125\t  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n126\t  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n127\t  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 = Jinja2) -> engine; file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler/lipsum/get_flashed_messages __globals__ os.popen, Twig source()/_self.env, ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also dump config (SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},\n128\t  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n129\t  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n130\t  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n131\t  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n132\t  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n133\t  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},\n134\t  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extension probing (shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a), filename traversal, SVG with script/XXE, template files if uploads are rendered. Payload only reads the prompt path. Parser: find the stored URL, fetch it, proof regex.\"},\n135\t  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n136\t  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n137\t  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length-diff oracle (bounded, [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars). Login bypass admin'--. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects.\"},\n138\t  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n139\t  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n140\t  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets).\"},\n141\t  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n142\t  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n143\t  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n144\t  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n145\t  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n146\t  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"}\n147\t]\n148\t```\n149\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a36620c-cc4e-43c4-b504-292458b62d8d","uuid":"32ca3d9e-643b-4fc5-a2f8-3edd0faaae38","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:09:30.600Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/web.md","content":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation. Since D05 every target is the same kit:\n`/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `current_role` + one concept key (`callback_nonce`,\n`moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`); routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece;\nsuccess = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Mastery = today's bug + 1-2 earlier lane-days\n(2 targets D03-D07, 3 on D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: ~3 lane-days per calendar day (D01-D03 cal.\n19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21) -> priority 1 below = the ~9 bugs most likely in D09-D17.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession management. D08 opened the auth/session family and D07 proved a real victim browser exists, so the next\nmost likely are: CSRF (bot victim), JWT / signed-cookie forgery, DOM XSS, open redirect, role tampering, then the\nserver-side classics (command injection, SSTI, SSRF, XXE, upload, deserialization).\nSnapshot 2026-10-21 (after D08). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and there is no `lib/web.py`; no `web:*` keys\nin `.run/prebuild-state.json` (gap `enable-web-prebuild-lane`).\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan\n`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie | flip the value the app names | high |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high (session family after D08) |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET only | add `role:\"admin\"` to PUT/POST | high |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | high |\n| 11 | SSTI | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | high |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | high |\n| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high (XSS trilogy) |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med-high |\n| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml` | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |\n| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med |\n| 20 | file upload -> execution / traversal | gap | upload form, files served back | executable type or `../` filename | med |\n| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med-low |\n| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n| 24a | CSRF (bot victim performs a state change) | gap | \"the admin clicks links\", \"change email\", no token / SameSite=None, report-to-admin | host an auto-submitting form / fetch in stored content or a bot-visited URL | high (bot proven D07; session family D08) |\n| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | med-high |\n| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker; bot reads data | med |\n| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |\n| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\" | parallel burst, negative values | med-low |\n| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint`, 400 `session_id_required` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie `arena_session=<hint>` on secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs/Referer | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med (D08 sequel) |\n| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ONE concept key (see table below)\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, 401/403 = needs the victim's/admin's session)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). JSON `evidence` = answer.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status, messages|postcards are re-dealt per variant).\nMASTERY: 2-3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty,\n      Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin: <base>, X-Callback-Nonce: N   -> effect isolated_browser_callback\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          {credentials:'include'}) -> POST RCPT(id from location.pathname)\n                                                            {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} and / for >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n\"admin clicks links\", \"change email\", report-to-admin  -> CSRF               -> stored/bot-visited auto-submit form to the state route\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read\n\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser required\" errors without a bot (D06) = send fetch-metadata headers yourself.\nBanners (\"Django\", \"Laravel\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python in a\nfuture `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded\nbodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no web prebuild lane).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D08: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and lib/web.py does not exist, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + JSON error codes to the concept and the next request (rows 5, 13a, 13b, 31)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"csrf-bot-planner\", \"concept\": \"CSRF executed by the app's victim bot (row 24a)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D07 proved the GM runs a real moderator browser. CSRF sequel: find the state-changing route (clues *_route, openapi POST/PUT without a token field, forms lacking csrf inputs, cookies SameSite=None/Lax), build (a) an auto-submitting HTML form (GET and POST, urlencoded and text/plain JSON trick) and (b) a fetch(...,{credentials:'include'}) script, deliver it where the bot looks (stored entry, report/share URL endpoint, profile field), then poll the clue/status route or the entry page for the receipt/effect. Token bypasses: drop the token, empty token, token from our own session, GET instead of POST, method override.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile route (mass assignment). Parser: effect+evidence JSON or proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 = Jinja2) -> engine; file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler/lipsum/get_flashed_messages __globals__ os.popen, Twig source()/_self.env, ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also dump config (SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extension probing (shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a), filename traversal, SVG with script/XXE, template files if uploads are rendered. Payload only reads the prompt path. Parser: find the stored URL, fetch it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length-diff oracle (bounded, [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars). Login bypass admin'--. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":149,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DQbsBDVWwmAueQGdFymkzC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
