min/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06 same-origin, D09 cross-site) = send\nthe Sec-Fetch-Site/Mode/Dest + Referer/Origin matrix yourself -- one request each, try before anything heavier.\nNEW CLASS = write a key-matched handler in solve.py before TT: the generic lib.web race missed D09 and D10 (~40 s).\"\"\")\nrep(\"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace).\",\n    \"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace).\")\nrep(\"None built yet (no web prebuild lane).\", \"None built yet (no web prebuild lane); D09 CSRF and D10 upload gaps dropped (seen).\")\n# JSON gaps\na=t.index(\"```json\\n\")+8; b=t.index(\"\\n```\",a)\ng=json.loads(t[a:b])\ng=[x for x in g if x[\"id\"] not in (\"csrf-bot-planner\",\"upload-execution-planner\")]\nby={x[\"id\"]:x for x in g}\nby[\"enable-web-prebuild-lane\"][\"detail\"]=\"Still true after D10: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/ now exists (handlers/__init__.py `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex -> `_HANDLERS`, `default` ladder; __init__.py races handlers + earlier days' answer()), so the lane's writable target is lib/web/handlers/ (one pure-ish handler per class) + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"\nby[\"xxe-payloads\"][\"priority\"]=1\nby[\"xxe-payloads\"][\"detail\"]+=\" D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"\nby[\"ssti-engine-probe\"][\"detail\"]=\"D10 preview already evaluated {{objective}} (a benign field lookup) -> a real SSTI day is the likeliest sequel. \"+by[\"ssti-engine-probe\"][\"detail\"]+\" Inject wherever the app renders user text: upload content (D10 shape), ?name=/?q= previews, profile fields; read the prompt path or an `objective`-style context var first ({{objective}}, {{config}}, {{self}}).\"\nby[\"clue-json-router\"][\"detail\"]+=\" Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"fetch-metadata-matrix\",\"concept\":\"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"upload-filter-bypass\",\"concept\":\"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"port-day22-handlers\",\"concept\":\"lib/web handlers for CSRF and upload (rows 20, 24a) + dead-target short-circuit\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Both day22 TTs returned solver_incomplete after ~41 s because lib.web had no handler for the new class and ran targets serially. Owner of lib/: port csrf() (challenges/day22/web-forged-with-care/solver/solve.py; _KEY_MAP r'preferences|csrf') and upload() (challenges/day22/web-uploading-expectations/solver/solve.py; r'upload|render|preview') into lib/web/handlers; make lib.web.main thread targets, accept pre-fetched clues, and skip the 40 s race when GET base is non-2xx/3xx (410 completed).\"},\n]\ng+=new\n# order: priority then keep\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x[\"priority\"])\nt=t[:a]+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nprint(sum(1 for x in g if x[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"), \"prebuild gaps\")\nEOF\npython3 -I -c \"\nimport json,re;t=open('reference/coverage/web.md').read();a=t.index('\\`\\`\\`json\\n')+8;b=t.index('\\n\\`\\`\\`',a);g=json.loads(t[a:b]);print(len(g),'ok',all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\ns=t.index('## Recognition cues');e=t.index('## Readiness gaps');print('cue lines',t[s:e].count('\\n'))\"; wc -l reference/coverage/web.md","description":"Update coverage atlas and validate JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":nul