n decorative. Routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece; success =\nJSON with `evidence: proof_...` (or the proof in a rendered page). Mastery = today's bug + 2 earlier lane-days (3\ntargets since D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21,\nD09-D10 cal. 22 (~2-3 lane-days per calendar day) -> priority 1 below = the bugs most likely in D11-D18.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload. The client-side/session block looks closed; D10 turned server-side and already\nshowed a template engine evaluating `{{objective}}`, so next most likely: SSTI, OS command injection, SSRF, XXE,\nJWT / signed-cookie forgery, role tampering / mass assignment, then open redirect, DOM XSS, deserialization.\nSnapshot 2026-10-22 (after D10). `lib/web/` now exists (`handlers/__init__.py`: `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex ->\nhandler, `_HANDLERS` = only `session_fixation`, plus a `default` ladder; `lib/web/__init__.py` races handlers +\nevery earlier web day's `answer()`; `hctf web-harden`). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys\nexist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap below is still pending.\n\n\"\"\"+t[j:]\nrep(\"Status legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib.\",\n    \"Status legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib (D09 `csrf()` / D10 `upload()` live only in their day22 solve.py, not lib).\")\nrep(\"| 11 | SSTI | gap | \\\"template\\\", \\\"preview\\\", \\\"greeting\\\", `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | high |\",\n    \"| 11 | SSTI | gap (D10 showed a `{{field}}` preview, benign lookup only) | \\\"template\\\", \\\"preview\\\", \\\"greeting\\\", `preview_guide`, `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | very high (D10 sequel) |\")\nrep(\"| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \\\"ping\\\", \\\"lookup host\\\", \\\"diagnostics\\\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | high |\",\n    \"| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \\\"ping\\\", \\\"lookup host\\\", \\\"diagnostics\\\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | very high (server-side turn) |\")\nrep(\"| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml` | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |\",\n    \"| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml`, `upload_shape` naming xml | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | high (upload kit exists) |\")\nrep(\"| 20 | file upload -> execution / traversal | gap | upload form, files served back | executable type or `../` filename | med |\",\n    \"| 20 | unrestricted upload rendered server-side | seen D10 (Mastery w/ D01+D02) | \\\"upload form has standards. Low ones\\\", `upload_shape`, `render_route`, `preview_guide`, `upload_policy` | POST JSON `{filename:x.html, content:<p>{{objective}}</p>, content_type:text/html}` -> GET returned `path` | done; Mastery |\\n| 20b | upload filter bypass / served-path traversal / stored SVG-HTML XSS | gap | policy actually enforced (`extension_not_allowed`, magic check), `../` in filename, uploads served raw | double ext, case, magic+type spoof, `../` filename, SVG script | med (D10 sequel) |\")\nrep(\"| 24a | CSRF (bot victim performs a state change) | gap | \\\"the admin clicks links\\\", \\\"change email\\\", no token / SameSite=None, report-to-admin | host an auto-submitting form / fetch in stored content or a bot-visited URL | high (bot proven D07; session family D08) |\",\n    \"| 24a | CSRF (state change \\\"as someone else\\\") | seen D09 | \\\"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\\\", \\\"forge one request\\\", `preferences_route`, form with hidden `csrf_token` | submit the form's external option with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`/`Mode: navigate`/`Dest: document` + foreign Referer; read `/api/preferences` | done; Mastery |\\n| 24e | CSRF sequels: token bound/checked, SameSite, JSON-body CSRF via bot | gap | token rejected when absent, `SameSite=Strict`, report-to-admin URL | token from own session, text/plain JSON form, GET-method downgrade, bot-delivered form | low-med |\")\n# cues block\nrep(\"\"\"session_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"session_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> GET / (arena_session), parse <form> on the page,\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             submit the non-current external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n                                                            cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, Referer: foreign\n                                                            (token optional); then GET /api/preferences -> evidence\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide/upload_policy  -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path; policy is costume\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"\"admin clicks links\", \"change email\", report-to-admin  -> CSRF               -> stored/bot-visited auto-submit form to the state route\\n\"\"\",\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read\"\"\",\n\"\"\"\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read (D10 guide = where to inject)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"A real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser required\" errors without a bot (D06) = send fetch-metadata headers yourself.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"A real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06 same-origin, D09 cross-site) = send\nthe Sec-Fetch-Site/Mode/Dest + Referer/Origin matrix yourself -- one request each, try before anything heavier.\nNEW CLASS = write a key-matched handler in solve.py before TT: the generic lib.web race missed D09 and D10 (~40 s).\"\"\")\nrep(\"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace).\",\n    \"Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace).\")\nrep(\"None built yet (no web prebuild lane).\", \"None built yet (no web prebuild lane); D09 CSRF and D10 upload gaps dropped (seen).\")\n# JSON gaps\na=t.index(\"```json\\n\")+8; b=t.index(\"\\n```\",a)\ng=json.loads(t[a:b])\ng=[x for x in g if x[\"id\"] not in (\"csrf-bot-planner\",\"upload-execution-planner\")]\nby={x[\"id\"]:x for x in g}\nby[\"enable-web-prebuild-lane\"][\"detail\"]=\"Still true after D10: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/ now exists (handlers/__init__.py `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex -> `_HANDLERS`, `default` ladder; __init__.py races handlers + earlier days' answer()), so the lane's writable target is lib/web/handlers/ (one pure-ish handler per class) + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"\nby[\"xxe-payloads\"][\"priority\"]=1\nby[\"xxe-payloads\"][\"detail\"]+=\" D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"\nby[\"ssti-engine-probe\"][\"detail\"]=\"D10 preview already evaluated {{objective}} (a benign field lookup) -> a real SSTI day is the likeliest sequel. \"+by[\"ssti-engine-probe\"][\"detail\"]+\" Inject wherever the app renders user text: upload content (D10 shape), ?name=/?q= previews, profile fields; read the prompt path or an `objective`-style context var first ({{objective}}, {{config}}, {{self}}).\"\nby[\"clue-json-router\"][\"detail\"]+=\" Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"fetch-metadata-matrix\",\"concept\":\"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"upload-filter-bypass\",\"concept\":\"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"port-day22-handlers\",\"concept\":\"lib/web handlers for CSRF and upload (rows 20, 24a) + dead-target short-circuit\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Both day22 TTs returned solver_incomplete after ~41 s because lib.web had no handler for the new class and ran targets serially. Owner of lib/: port csrf() (challenges/day22/web-forged-with-care/solver/solve.py; _KEY_MAP r'preferences|csrf') and upload() (challenges/day22/web-uploading-expectations/solver/solve.py; r'upload|render|preview') into lib/web/handlers; make lib.web.main thread targets, accept pre-fetched clues, and skip the 40 s race when GET base is non-2xx/3xx (410 completed).\"},\n]\ng+=new\n# order: priority then keep\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x[\"priority\"])\nt=t[:a]+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nprint(sum(1 for x in g if x[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"), \"prebuild gaps\")\nEOF\npython3 -I -c \"\nimport json,re;t=open('reference/coverage/web.md').read();a=t.index('\\`\\`\\`json\\n')+8;b=t.index('\\n\\`\\`\\`',a);g=json.loads(t[a:b]);print(len(g),'ok',all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\ns=t.index('## Recognition cues');e=t.index('## Readiness gaps');print('cue lines',t[s:e].count('\\n'))\"; wc -l reference/coverage/web.md","description":"Update coverage atlas and validate JSON"}}}
